  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Robust Interventions to Combat Human Trafficking in Mexico</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The overarching vision of this project is to enhance Mexico&#x2019;s national, state, and local-level TIP responses particularly for migrants, displaced populations, and other vulnerable groups (including children), to support the country&#x2019;s path toward achievement of Tier 1 status.  The key goal of the project is to increase identification and protection of VoT, particularly among migrants at the U.S.-Mexico border and elsewhere.The project targets key areas on the U.S-Mexico and southern Mexico border and the Metropolitan Area of the Valley of Mexico, specifically in the following 5 states: Baja California, Chihuahua, Mexico City, the State of Mexico, and Chiapas &#x2013; and 8 cities &#x2013; Tijuana (San Ysidro area), Mexicali, Ciudad Ju&#xe1;rez, Chihuahua, Toluca, Mexico City, Tuxtla Gutierrez, and Tapachula. These areas possess some of the highest levels of detected cases of trafficking and represent areas where 3P response capacities are currently overrun considering the sheer volume and presence of highly vulnerable groups, underdeveloped capacities of frontline actors, and a lack of local coordination between CT actors, among others.</narrative>
  </description>
